    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '113007J';

UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<h4>Course overview</h4><p>Our two-year Master of Teaching program qualifies you to be a teacher in Australia, and many countries overseas. Teaching is a career in which you can make a positive and life-long impact on the lives of children and young people. You can choose to specialise in early childhood education, primary education, or secondary education. Please see below for availabilities and start dates for each specialisation. As well as undertaking an education research project, this course includes professional experience learning via placement in early childhood education settings, schools, and/or community sites of a total 480 hours (60 days). Pre-requisites to meet national and state-based regulatory requirements, as detailed in Faculty of Education Professional Experience Requirements, must be met prior to attending professional experience placement. All professional experience learning days must be completed, and professional behaviour and conduct must be demonstrated. Primary and Secondary Initial Teacher Education students across Australia need to attempt the Literacy and Numeracy Test for Initial Teacher Education Students (LANTITE) in their first year of study and successfully complete the LANTITE. Early Childhood Initial Teacher Education students do not have to do the LANTITE. Undertaking full-time study may be required from January to December (6 teaching terms) depending on your program of study. From 2026, Southern Cross University’s Initial Teacher Education (ITE) courses no longer require applicants to complete a non-academic selection statement. This change reflects a national update to the Initial Teacher Education Accreditation Standards and has been approved by the NSW Education Standards Authority (NESA) for all SCU ITE programs. Please note, primary and secondary education require the completion of previous studies related to teaching areas. For secondary, if you have not already completed these studies, you may be required to complete additional units as part of your degree. Students who commenced their studies in Term 3 or Term 5 of 2025, or in Term 1 of 2026, and request to transfer to the Graduate Diploma of Teaching (GDTeach) may only do so after the successful completion of the first year of the Master of Teaching (MTeach) program, specialising in either Primary or Secondary Education. This first year includes eight coursework units and a 30-day professional experience placement. Following the transfer to the GDTeach, students are required to undertake an additional 15-day professional experience placement. In total, a minimum of 45 days of professional experience is necessary to meet the GDTeach course requirements. Students who commence in Term 3 2026 onwards and request to transfer to the Graduate Diploma of Teaching (Primary, Secondary) are advised to transfer to the GDTeach before commencing their first professional experience unit in the Master of Teaching (Primary, Secondary) program. Reimagining Teacher Education Project – available for the first time in 2026 A new project launching in 2026 will offer Master of Teaching students the opportunity to combine their studies with two days of in-school experience every week. There are fifty places available in Diocese of Lismore Catholic Schools. Learn more</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 52000,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = 4000,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '',
    apply_form = 'https://www.scu.edu.au/study/courses/master-of-teaching-1209001/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '110587H';

